        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "B.7.3 Common requirements for OEM provisioning certificate profiles",
            "block_bbox": [
                70,
                395,
                789,
                422
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    70.0,
                    395.0
                ],
                [
                    789.0,
                    395.0
                ],
                [
                    789.0,
                    422.0
                ],
                [
                    70.0,
                    422.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "As mentioned in Table B.11 and Table B.12 it is optional to include the \"certificatePolicies\" extension in any of the OEM provisioning certificates. If the \"certificatePolicies\" extension is included, it can be marked as non-critical so that the relying party can ignore this extension if it cannot process it. This is done to improve the interoperability.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                444,
                1054,
                550
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    444.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    444.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    550.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    550.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "It should be noted that neither EVCC nor SECC validate the OEM provisioning certificate or any other certificates included in that chain. The EVCC provides this certificate to the eMSP during CertificateInstallationReq. It is up to the eMSP to validate the certificate and ensure it meets the requirements.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                571,
                1054,
                677
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    571.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    571.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    677.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    677.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "When the configurable mechanism as defined by [V2G20-2320] indicates that the curve as defined by [V2G20-2319] needs to be used, the EVCC will send its OEM provisioning certificate conforming to Table B.11 to the eMSP via the SECC. When the configurable mechanism as defined by [V2G20-2320] indicates that the curve as defined by [V2G20-2674] needs to be used, the EVCC will send its OEM provisioning certificate conforming to Table B.12 to the eMSP via the SECC. When the eMSP receives an OEM provisioning certificate conforming to Table B.12, it will use SubjectPublicKey defined in Table B.11 for ECDHE per 7.9.2.5.4. When the eMSP receives an OEM provisioning certificate conforming to Table B.12, it will use subjectAltPublicKey defined in Table B.12 for ECDHE per 7.9.2.5.4.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                699,
                1054,
                908
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    699.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    699.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    908.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    908.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-1780] PCID shall be created per C.2.",
            "block_bbox": [
                70,
                929,
                539,
                956
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    70.0,
                    929.0
                ],
                [
                    539.0,
                    929.0
                ],
                [
                    539.0,
                    956.0
                ],
                [
                    70.0,
                    956.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-1781] PCID shall be contained in the subject field of the provisioning certificate as follows:",
            "block_bbox": [
                70,
                979,
                1048,
                1006
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    70.0,
                    979.0
                ],
                [
                    1048.0,
                    979.0
                ],
                [
                    1048.0,
                    1006.0
                ],
                [
                    70.0,
                    1006.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- the PCID itself (see [V2G20-1780]) shall be the value of the common name (CN) of the distinguished name (DN);",
            "block_bbox": [
                280,
                1012,
                1050,
                1061
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    280.0,
                    1012.0
                ],
                [
                    1050.0,
                    1012.0
                ],
                [
                    1050.0,
                    1061.0
                ],
                [
                    280.0,
                    1061.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- the name of the OEM shall be encoded in the field organization (O) using a unique identifier chosen by the OEM, to identify this OEM;",
            "block_bbox": [
                283,
                1064,
                1051,
                1113
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    283.0,
                    1064.0
                ],
                [
                    1051.0,
                    1064.0
                ],
                [
                    1051.0,
                    1113.0
                ],
                [
                    283.0,
                    1113.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- the X.500 distinguished name in the subject field shall not contain any further values.",
            "block_bbox": [
                282,
                1116,
                1052,
                1166
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
